    "module_designation": "Digital indicating device",
    "description": "The RW-5002PL digital indicating device (part of the RW-5000 Series) connected to two independent weighing platforms (weigh pads) to form a single or dual-interval, Class III or IIII, weighing instrument. Portable, self-indicating and battery-powered; shall not be used for direct sales to the public. Main features: plastic enclosure, LCD display, alphanumeric keypad and function keys, integrated printer, dual channel (two load cell connections), 7-pin load cell connectors. Devices: initial zero setting device on power up, semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking (optional), zero-indicator, indication of stable equilibrium, gravity compensation, printing, totalisation of weights, load identification register. The summation of axle weights is not permitted under this certificate. Interfaces: load cell connection, RS232/485, USB (optional). Any compatible load cell may be used provided it holds an OIML R60 Certificate of Conformity containing the necessary data for the manufacturer's declaration of compatibility of modules; a load cell marked NH is allowed only if humidity testing to R76 has been conducted on it. Software is held in firmware with identification number V1.xx and is sealed; access to legally relevant parameters is prevented by a jumper on the main board. Sealing is by tamper-evident method."
  },
